+### Qualified local text helpers (opt-in, no fallback)
+
+For already-qualified local models, `title_generation`, `profile_describer` and the
+tool-free `scripts/local_helper.py` entry point support a separate **local-only**
+policy. This does not qualify a model, spawn a child agent, change the parent model,
+or enable a route automatically. Unconfigured users retain the ordinary routing
+and fallback behavior. Have the supervising parent validate the model's suitability
+for each role before enabling it; helper text is untrusted, never an approval or a
+security-review verdict.
+
+Configure a task through the supported CLI (repeat for each accepted task):
+
+```bash
+hermes config set auxiliary.title_generation.provider llama.cpp
+hermes config set auxiliary.title_generation.model YOUR_QUALIFIED_MODEL_ALIAS
+hermes config set auxiliary.title_generation.base_url http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1
+hermes config set auxiliary.title_generation.fallback_enabled false
+```
+
+The pin must name `llama.cpp`, `llama-cpp` or `llamacpp`, a nonempty literal model
+other than `auto`, and an explicit HTTP endpoint at `127.0.0.1` or `[::1]` with a
+canonical port (1–65535). Only the root or `/v1` path (optional trailing slash on
+`/v1`) is supported. Hostnames, alternate IP spellings, HTTPS, credentials in
+URLs, query strings, fragments, redirects and arbitrary paths are refused.
+`custom`, named custom providers, `auto`, managed-server discovery without an
+endpoint, and cloud providers are not supported by this policy.
+When the main model shares the local server, use the same canonical base URL
+spelling for both routes so existing title deferral recognizes the shared endpoint.
+
+`fallback_enabled: false` is a strict boolean opt-in. Invalid pins and unsupported
+tasks fail before generic provider/credential resolution. There are no retries,
+cloud fallbacks, ambient credentials/headers, proxy-environment routing, inherited
+`extra_body`, or Relay request rewrites. Only bounded `model`, text `messages` and
+`max_tokens` fields go on the wire. Configured API keys, credential selectors
+(`key_env`/`api_key_env`), and wire controls are
+refused. The fixed title schema/thinking-off controls are accepted only from the
+title caller, checked locally and not forwarded; the profile caller's fixed
+temperature hint is likewise not forwarded. Choose a model/server whose default
+behavior suits these short tasks; the helper does not change server defaults.
+An unreadable or malformed settings file refuses these three tasks, including
+when the loader offers defaults or last-known-good settings; fix the file rather
+than relying on an implicit return to ordinary routing.
+
+Each supported task registers these defaults under `local_helper_caps`; they
+apply only to local-only calls, independently of the ordinary task `timeout`:
+
+| Setting | Default | Hard limit |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| `timeout` | 15 seconds | finite 0.05–30 seconds, **one absolute deadline**, including queue/send/receive |
+| `max_tokens` | 512 | positive integer, at most 1024 |
+| `max_input_chars` | 16384 | positive integer, at most 32768 across all messages |
+| `max_response_bytes` | 65536 | positive integer, at most 131072 raw bytes |
+
+Requests are also limited to 32 plain-text messages and 128 KiB serialized JSON.
+Response text is additionally limited to 16 characters per requested output
+token (a text-size guard, not a tokenizer). All compressed responses are refused
+before decoding; malformed, empty, truncated, refused, wrong-model or tool-call
+responses fail without fallback. Every connection is closed. Existing profile/task
+concurrency budgets remain in use (sync and async budgets are separate, as before);
+the local-only default is one permit, with `max_concurrency` restricted to integer
+values 1–8 (not strings). Async permits are owned only by live requests/waiters;
+their weak cache neither retains closed event loops nor reuses recycled loop IDs.
+Observers receive copies, not writable transport payloads.
+Per-call limits must fit the task caps. The title caller requests 512 output
+tokens and the profile caller requests 400, so lowering their respective caps
+below those values refuses the calls; limits are never silently widened.
+Profile description now honors its configured task timeout when no explicit
+timeout is supplied, rather than overriding it with a fixed 60 seconds.
+
+Stateless Python `run_oneshot` and `llm.oneshot` RPC requests default to the
+separate `auxiliary.oneshot` task (ordinary routing, parent model by default).
+Local-only title routing therefore does not capture commit-message or idea
+requests with their different temperature/token/time budgets. If you previously
+used `auxiliary.title_generation` to configure one-shots, move those settings to
+`auxiliary.oneshot`; explicit task overrides still obey the selected task's
+policy. `oneshot` is not eligible for this credential-free local-only policy.
+
+Enable `auxiliary.local_helper` separately, then use the script with the installed
+Hermes interpreter from the source checkout:
+
+```bash
+python scripts/local_helper.py --instruction 'Summarize this non-sensitive note' < note.txt
+```
+
+The script reads bounded text from stdin and returns one untrusted text result.
+Terminal controls (except newline/tab) and lone surrogates are rendered as visible
+Unicode escapes; input/output encoding failures return a controlled error without
+echoing the data or a traceback.
+It has no tools, no conversation history, no provider/model override, and no
+fallback when unconfigured. Do not send secrets or use it for compression,
+vision, approval, or security review. Restoring `fallback_enabled: true` restores
+ordinary routing for title/profile calls, including possible cloud traffic; it
+does **not** allow the standalone script to use cloud routing.
+
 ### Stream-only endpoints
 
 Some OpenAI-compatible endpoints reject non-streaming chat requests outright (e.g. Tencent Copilot returns HTTP 400 `"Non-stream chat request is currently not supported"`). Interactive chat already streams, but auxiliary tasks (title generation, compression, vision) use non-streaming calls and would fail on every attempt. Hermes always treats `copilot.tencent.com` as stream-only; for any other such endpoint, list a URL substring under `auxiliary.stream_only_base_urls`:
